  "question": {
    "text": "The statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a tautology",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a contradiction",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using logical equivalence condition&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;given statement can be expressed as,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>We know De Morgan&#39;s law of logical equivalence is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>Applying De Morgan&#39;s law in equation(1) we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;(tautology)</p>"
  }
